# Transformation Board — the daily pulse (CFO 2026-09-20).
#
# "create a living dashboard which updates everyday linking to our everyday
# activities and software development". This is the job that makes it living:
# every morning it recomputes the board from live payroll, the Build Log,
# tasks, Time Doctor and the per-day workday record, refreshes each
# department's headcount and cost, asks the AI panel for the morning note, and
# stores ONE snapshot for the day so the screen can animate a real trend.
#
# Drop this file into /etc/cron.d/ on the omni EC2 (sudo cp + chmod 644).
# System clock is UTC. SAST/CAT = UTC+02.
#
#   03:40 UTC (05:40 CAT) — before anyone opens the board for the day, and
#   after the overnight jobs (Time Doctor pull, bank feeds, watchdogs) have
#   finished, so the morning note reads last night's real work.
#
# READ-MOSTLY: the only writes are the day's snapshot and each department's
# refreshed headcount/cost. It posts no journal, moves no money, sends no
# customer mail, and never writes to Graphite.
#
# If the AI panel is unreachable the figures are unaffected — the board simply
# has no paragraph that morning (see transformation/ai_panel.py).
#
# Output -> /var/log/alpha-finance/transformation-pulse.log (root-owned).

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

40 3 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/bin/docker compose --env-file /etc/alpha-finance/.env exec -T backend python manage.py transformation_pulse --commit >> /var/log/alpha-finance/transformation-pulse.log 2>&1
